Subject: [PATCH] orangepi4pro: cap NPU at 852MHz (shared 0.8V DCDC2 rail)

On the OPi 4 Pro, VDD-NPU sits on the AXP8191 DCDC2 rail, shared with HDMI/DRAM/
UFS/both combo-PHYs and pinned at 0.8V. The NPU 1008/1120MHz OPPs need 0.96V+,
unreachable on this board, so the driver runs 1008MHz undervolted and produces
intermittent silent compute errors (seen via vpm_run golden-compare). Cap at 852MHz
(top 0.8V OPP) in the board dts (not the shared SoC cpu-vf dtsi, so Radxa/other A733
boards are unaffected).

Two changes, one cap that serves both NPU drivers:
 - Delete opp-1008/opp-1120: this is what caps vipcore (VIPLite path), which ignores
   npu-vf and otherwise selects the top OPP. Validated on HW: 10000/10000 vipcore
   golden compares pass at 852MHz.
 - Retarget npu-vf to 852 (0x354): galcore (Unified/OpenVX path) is OPP-exact -- it
   reads npu-vf and requires that exact OPP node, so without this it can't find its
   target OPP (npu-vf default 0x3f0=1008 is deleted) and falls back to an unmanaged
   clock. Harmless to vipcore.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-4-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-4-pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-4-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-4-pro.dts
@@ -2665,6 +2665,19 @@ &npu {
 	status = "okay";
 };

+/* VDD-NPU shares the 0.8V DCDC2 rail (HDMI/DRAM/UFS/combo-PHYs), so it can't reach the
+ * 0.96V the 1008MHz OPP needs; cap at 852MHz (top 0.8V OPP) to avoid undervolt errors.
+ * galcore is OPP-exact (reads npu-vf, requires that exact OPP node), so also retarget
+ * npu-vf to 852; vipcore ignores npu-vf and caps via the deleted OPPs -- one cap, both drivers. */
+&npu {
+	npu-vf = <0x354>;	/* 852MHz */
+};
+
+&npu_opp_table {
+	/delete-node/ opp-1008;
+	/delete-node/ opp-1120;
+};
+
 &addr_mgt {
 	compatible     = "allwinner,sunxi-addr_mgt";
 	type_addr_wifi = <0x0>;
